= Addressing the Economic Crisis

Our party is wracked as to how to deal with the economic crisis. From the centrist faction, Brüning argues that fiscal orthodoxy is required in order to prevent inflation. Across bourgeois spheres, ideas of financial expert and economist Wilhelm Lautenbach - the so-called "Lautenbach Plan" is gaining popularity, advocating for public works programs funded by wage reductions.
[? if wtb_conceptualized: However, leftists in the party argue that the Lautenbach plan will cause too much suffering among the workers, instead calling for the newly conceptualized <span style="color: #000000;">W</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">T</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">B</span>-Plan, named after the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Socialist**</span> economists Woytinsky, Tarnow, and Baade, promoting aggresive deficit spending to stimulate the economy. ?]

- @support_centrist: Support Austerity.
- @support_lautenbach: Support the Lautenbach Plan.
- @defer: Defer making a decision until we have more information.

@support_centrist
subtitle: Austerity politics to stop economic chaos.
on-arrival: center_strength += 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent += 10; wtb_support -= 1; left_dissent += 10;

Leftists and the trade unions vehemently criticize the centrists for their policy. The workers are starving; are we going to further their suffering with austerity? On the other hand, the centrists criticize labor for their recklessness; their position is that goverment spending will further worsen the crisis. They also speak of the fear of another round of hyperinflation that may result from deficit spending.

Our policy course is currently that nothing can be done to alleviate the depression.

@support_lautenbach
subtitle: Call for increased public works and fiscal stimulus.
unavailable-subtitle: The Labor faction is not strong enough.
choose-if: labor_strength >= left_strength and labor_strength >= center_strength
view-if: wtb_concept
on-arrival: center_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 5; labor_strength += 5; wtb_support += 1; wtb_points += 10

Our support of the WTB plan alienates the orthodox economics of the Centrist faction, and faces both opposition and support from a variety of sources across the spectrum.

We have not yet convinced the party to formally adopt the plan. More work needs to be done.

@defer

We hold off on making a decision on economic policy, awaiting more information. Woytinsky and his supporters argue that inaction is a form of action of its own. 
